<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>cercano-agent</id>
    <version>@VERSION@</version>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/cercano-ai/Cercano/tree/main/release/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <title>Cercano Agent</title>
    <authors>Cercano contributors</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/cercano-ai/Cercano</projectUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/cercano-ai/Cercano@v@VERSION@/website/app/icon.svg</iconUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/cercano-ai/Cercano/blob/v@VERSION@/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <docsUrl>https://github.com/cercano-ai/Cercano/tree/v@VERSION@/docs</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/cercano-ai/Cercano/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <tags>cercano agent ai llm coding-agent cli foss</tags>
    <summary>The Cercano agent (cercano.exe), which runs models and tools for Cercano clients.</summary>
    <description>Cercano is a free and open agent and harness: use frontier providers through a subscription sign-in or API key, run open-weight models, or combine them, with routing, delegation and context management built in.

This package installs the agent, `cercano.exe`, and its `cercano` command. Install `cercano-cli` (or the `cercano` package for both) to use it from a terminal.

- Close Cercano before upgrading or uninstalling: the package refuses while any of its processes run, and never stops them for you.
- The executable is not code signed, so Windows may show a SmartScreen warning.
- A local model runtime is not bundled.</description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/cercano-ai/Cercano/releases/tag/v@VERSION@</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
